<title>FINLAND: Silja Line July passenger vol falls 2 pct.</title>
<headline>Silja Line July passenger vol falls 2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish passenger ferry operator Silja Oy Ab said in a statement on Friday that the number of passengers carried in July by its Baltic Sea operator Silja Line fell by two percent year-on-year to 805,000 passengers.  </p>
<p> Passenger volume	     July 1997    Change 96/97</p>
<p>  (1,000)					    (percent)</p>
<p> Helsinki-Stockholm		   158		+2</p>
<p> Turku-Stockholm			260		-3</p>
<p> Vaasa traffic			  222		+9</p>
<p> Mariehamn traffic		     35		+1</p>
<p> Helsinki-Tallinn			93	     -21</p>
<p> Helsinki-Travemunde		   37		+1</p>
<p> TOTAL passengers		     805		-2</p>
<p> Freight units			   10	     +15</p>
<p>Silja said Silja Line's passenger volume in January-July fell two percent year-on-year to 3.48 million passengers.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
